  "name": null,
  "problem": "A thread manufacturer tests the tensile strength of a sample containing $9$ pieces of a particular type of thread.\nThe mean tensile strength of the sample is $7.8\\,\\text{lb}$ with a standard deviation of $0.06\\,\\text{lb}.$\nAssuming that tensile strengths are normally distributed, find a $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean tensile strength  $\\mu $ of this thread. \n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $T$ that has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom, the table below shows the $t$-scores ${t}_{k,p}$ such that $P(T>{t}_{k,p})=p$ for some particular values of $k$ and $p.$*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $7$ | $\\,1.415\\,$ | $\\,1.895\\,$ | $\\,2.365\\,$ | $\\,2.998\\,$ | $\\,3.499\\,$ |\n| $8$ | $\\,1.397\\,$ | $\\,1.860\\,$ | $\\,2.306\\,$ | $\\,2.896\\,$ | $\\,3.355\\,$ |\n| $9$ | $\\,1.383\\,$ | $\\,1.833\\,$ | $\\,2.262\\,$ | $\\,2.821\\,$ | $\\,3.250\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
